{"id": "EUVD-2026-11703", "enisaUuid": "6a157401-2a53-300d-81fb-fef3a49eb4c4", "description": "ImpactA server can reply with a WebSocket frame using the 64-bit length form and an extremely large length. undici's ByteParser overflows internal math, ends up in an invalid state, and throws a fatal TypeError that terminates the process.\n\nPatches\n\nPatched in the undici version v7.24.0 and v6.24.0. Users should upgrade to this version or later.", "datePublished": "2026-03-12T20:21:57", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-14T12:04:20", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://github.com/nodejs/undici/security/advisories/GHSA-f269-vfmq-vjvj", "https://hackerone.com/reports/3537648", "https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html"], "aliases": ["GHSA-f269-vfmq-vjvj", "CVE-2026-1528"], "assigner": "openjs", "epss": 0.5, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "b9172124-27e7-3290-a3e1-63e8d3078fde", "product": {"name": "undici", "vendor": {"name": "undici"}}, "product_version": "6.0.0 < 6.24.0; 7.0.0 < 7.24.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "74f4cfc8-12ae-3a47-9cc9-ab8e90822614", "vendor": {"name": "undici"}}], "isExploited": false}